WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.640
During the Purge, all crime is legal, so this&nbsp;
isn’t even a question right? You should definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.720
be able to steal stuff. The answer isn’t that&nbsp;
simple. If you Purge someone during The Purge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.200
the whole act is concluded before The Purge ends.&nbsp;
But The Purge Season 2 shows us that if you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.680
still on private property after the conclusion of&nbsp;
the last siren, they can book you for trespassing.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.000
So what if you steal something? Are you required&nbsp;
to drop it before the end of the final siren? Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.920
it considered possession of stolen property the&nbsp;
moment the 12 hours of the Purge have elapsed?

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.280
If you’re watching this on the day of&nbsp;
upload, Happy Purge to each and every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.800
one of you. My initial plan for today’s&nbsp;
festivities was to upload my Things You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.240
Missed episode on The Purge TV series --&nbsp;
however that’s gonna take a little bit longer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.360
but I couldn’t leave you with no&nbsp;
Purge video on Purge night, so....

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.120
Before you head out there and do your own&nbsp;
purging, it’s best to know and understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.000
the rules, and I’ve been seeing this&nbsp;
question a lot in my comments lately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.200
If you steal something during The Purge, do&nbsp;
you get to keep it? The answer is… sometimes.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.040
[INTRO]

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.960
To answer this question, let's look back at&nbsp;
things that have been stolen during The Purge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.120
In the original movie, Mrs. Sandin hangs the&nbsp;
Polite Stranger’s rifle after he is purged,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.200
but Dante Bishop gives back the gun that he&nbsp;
acquired from The Sandins, though this could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.280
just be because the family had already lost&nbsp;
so much and he wasn’t gonna take anything else.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.440
In Anarchy, Leo, Cali and Eva steal weapons&nbsp;
and a vehicle from the woman who hosted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.040
the Purge gala. Leo leaves the girls in the&nbsp;
car while he goes to take care of business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.040
but he’s critically injured just before&nbsp;
The Purge ends. Before the sirens sound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.200
Eva and Cali get out of the car to go aid him,&nbsp;
but they hang onto the guns. It’s safe to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.960
at this point that stolen guns can be kept, but&nbsp;
when they’re trying to get Leo to the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.920
they don’t seem to consider using&nbsp;
the stolen car they were just in.
 &nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.337
EVA: “You got a car?”
WARREN: “Uh.”&nbsp;

00:01:40.337 --> 00:01:41.302
EVA: “You got a f***ing car?”&nbsp;

00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:42.560
WARREN: “Yes.”
EVA: “GO GET IT NOW!”

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.680
So they use this guy’s car to get&nbsp;
Leo to the hospital. It seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.240
cars cannot be kept if stolen during The Purge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.560
We don’t see anything else get stolen during&nbsp;
Anarchy, but we can learn more from this line.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.760
LIZ: “It’s so quiet here.”
LEO: “Business district’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.280
always quiet on Purge night, the banks move&nbsp;
their money, so no one’s ever down here.”

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.040
The fact that the banks move their money suggests&nbsp;
that there is an incentive for someone to try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.640
rob the bank, which does happen in a&nbsp;
later installment. We’ll get to that.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.560
Next is Election Year. The main story ends&nbsp;
just after midnight, so we never actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.160
see the end of that Purge, however there&nbsp;
is an item that is attempted to be stolen.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.120
“I want my candy bar. And I’m gonna take it!”

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.360
Yeahhh… Kimmy tries to steal a candy bar.&nbsp;
I think we can all agree it’s no surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.880
that this would be allowed, especially&nbsp;
if you eat it before Purge ends. Marcos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.800
comes back after the conclusion and finds the&nbsp;
whole deli ransacked, so it seems likely that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.720
any food items are fair game to keep after&nbsp;
The Purge, regardless of if they are eaten.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.680
Another note to make about Election&nbsp;
Year -- it takes place in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.480
and Dante is still easily able to hotwire a car,&nbsp;
which he only uses for a moment before his death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.680
But my takeaway from this, is that&nbsp;
it’s not difficult to steal a car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.360
so the fact that The Purge hasn’t become&nbsp;
a free-for-all for every parked car on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.320
street must mean that you can’t&nbsp;
keep a vehicle if you steal one.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.920
The fourth movie is the prequel, The First&nbsp;
Purge. This time we actually get to see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.520
couple robberies take place. One man&nbsp;
attempts to pry open an ATM machine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.480
If you’re not allowed to keep the money you&nbsp;
steal during the Purge, he has no reason to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.720
be out there risking his life. We also see a&nbsp;
group of thieves target a cash for gold store.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:12.480
“I’m exercising my right to Purge by taking all&nbsp;
your merch, and if you stand in my way I will f***&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:17.280
you up! Let’s f***ing Purge y’all!"

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.680
This place has jewelry, guns, gold and&nbsp;
silver. They’re stealing more valuable items,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.920
which tells me that what can and cannot be kept&nbsp;
probably isn’t so much related to the price tag.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.520
So far it seems like cars cannot be kept&nbsp;
post-purge, but any items small enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.800
hold in your hand are fair game, including money.&nbsp;
What about larger sums of money or larger objects?

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.360
While The Purge Season 1 does&nbsp;
not have much thieving going on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.400
Season 2 introduces us to a band of bank robbers.&nbsp;
What happens is interesting. Three of them make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.920
it out of the bank before Purge ends, and&nbsp;
they get to keep their money. But Tommy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.160
gets caught with his foot on the line as time&nbsp;
expires, and they book him for armed robbery.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.240
However, they later find out that they amount they&nbsp;
stole wasn’t actually that much, because the banks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.760
are keeping most of their money in an airplane&nbsp;
throughout the entire duration of The Purge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.600
so next Purge they come up with a plan to prevent&nbsp;
the plane from taking off, and take in a haul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:06.160
upwards of 100 million dollars, proving that&nbsp;
the value of products stolen is not a factor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.240
The money is kept in these huge rolling cases&nbsp;
which they unload from an armored truck onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.480
their boat. This has me convinced that the size&nbsp;
of an item isn’t necessarily relevant here either.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.840
Their plan was always to stop the plane&nbsp;
from taking off. They never seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.680
consider hijacking the plane. Maybe there are&nbsp;
practical reasons that they couldn’t do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.760
but the fact stands that the idea of trying to&nbsp;
stow away in one of these cases and take control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.400
of the plane is never even brought up. Which leads&nbsp;
me to believe that planes are also off limits.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.960
But there is perhaps an even more important&nbsp;
detail I noticed in Season 2 that answers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.040
another previously unknown question. What&nbsp;
about houses? Can you take over someone's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.320
home or business, purge the inhabitants&nbsp;
and claim it as your own property?

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.160
Season 2's story revolves around the death&nbsp;
of a character named Drew Adams. Her friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.080
Esme stops by her house after she&nbsp;
is gone and encounters two realtors.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.520
“I’m so sorry. We’re just doing a first&nbsp;
inspection. Did you want to look around?”&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.400
“Or are you thinking of buying? The owner was&nbsp;
just purged and we think it’s gonna go very fast.”

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.280
It would appear that if a person&nbsp;
is purged, their home can’t be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.640
claimed -- instead it just goes on the&nbsp;
market. This is kind of a dark detail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.160
the NFFA can just purge people and&nbsp;
turn a huge profit on their house.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.800
So you can't keep real estate or vehicles.&nbsp;
If you steal a car, have fun on your joyride,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:17.040
but you better be out of it by 7:00AM.&nbsp;
Same goes for real estate. But you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.480
keep other items or money, no matter&nbsp;
how big, no matter how valuable.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.560
So what is the logic behind these&nbsp;
rules? I think I have the answer.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:36.560
All crime is legal during the Purge. You cannot&nbsp;
go back and try to arrest someone after The Purge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.880
for a crime that was committed during The Purge. However,&nbsp;
if that crime is still happening when The Purge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:44.560
concludes, it’s considered an off-Purge crime.&nbsp;
That’s why Tommy is arrested for still being at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.760
the bank. If I steal $5 from you, it’s my money&nbsp;
now, as long as I steal it during The Purge.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:55.120
Money, weapons, jewelry, food and other common&nbsp;
items are transferred by hand to hand exchange.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.680
For example, if you give someone&nbsp;
a cookie, it’s assumed that you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.880
giving them ownership. Even if it’s agreed&nbsp;
that they’re just borrowing the cookie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.920
it’s ultimately going to be on&nbsp;
them to return it. You voluntarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.680
gave the cookie to them -- so no crime was&nbsp;
committed even if they don’t give it back.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.160
However, that’s not how you transfer vehicles or&nbsp;
real estate. If I wanted to transfer ownership of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.680
my car to you, which I don’t, what do I look&nbsp;
like David Dobrik? -- I’d have to fill out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.560
title certificate, sign it, and go to the local&nbsp;
DMV to officially transfer the ownership. The DMV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.720
is not open during the Purge, so transferring&nbsp;
ownership is impossible. Meaning when I wake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.600
up on March 22nd the car still belongs to me&nbsp;
no matter what happened in the last 12 hours.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.120
Even if the car title is stolen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.040
the DMV has a duplicate, which they can&nbsp;
still give a copy of to the legal owner.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.040
“For, eh, a small fee.”

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:41.280
There is a similar process for transferring&nbsp;
real-estate. Once again, you have a title as proof&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.880
of your legal ownership. You need to have to get&nbsp;
a real-estate attorney who will prepare the deed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.000
the legal document that transfers ownership&nbsp;
of the property. You’ll need to sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.560
the deed in front of a notary, a public&nbsp;
officer who is not available on Purge night.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.280
These processes also apply to aircrafts, boats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.200
trailers, businesses and probably&nbsp;
submarines. I mean, I didn’t look it up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:04.000
but I’m guessing submarines. So the Purge&nbsp;
isn’t useful for stealing these kinds of items.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.400
You may be wondering, OK, what if I just use&nbsp;
The Purge to steal a car, hide it in a garage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.200
then sell it off the record for cash or for parts?&nbsp;
Sure, you’d be committing a crime, but because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.120
there are no emergency services during The Purge,&nbsp;
there’s a good chance you’d get away with it.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.640
Well, that’s not so easy either.&nbsp;
The Purge takes place in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.160
and we already have modern vehicles that&nbsp;
are practically impossible to steal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:28.880
two factor authentication. However, based on how&nbsp;
easily Dante hacks the car in Election Year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.240
let’s just assume the criminals have&nbsp;
evolved as fast as auto security.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.240
Even then, you’re not gonna get very far.&nbsp;
Dante drove the car all of 20 feet before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.000
getting purged. With GPS tracking, stolen&nbsp;
cars are becoming a thing of the past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.120
Even if you’re an experienced&nbsp;
hacker and managed to disable this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.480
good luck relocating the car when&nbsp;
nearly every street in America is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:50.480
covered by cameras and watched over&nbsp;
by a team of NFFA surveillance agents.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:55.040
So your best bet is going after that cold&nbsp;
hard cash. Or a candy bar. Man’s gotta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.840
eat. If you have other questions&nbsp;
about The Purge, drop a comment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.080
and maybe I’ll answer in a future video. Check&nbsp;
out my purge playlist on the left and remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:07.040
to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every&nbsp;
week, ring the deathbell for ALL notifications,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.480
and I’ll see you in the next purge. Assuming we&nbsp;
both survive. If you don’t want to get purged,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:17.801
stay home. If you have to go out for essentials, wear&nbsp;
a mask.

